<title>SWEDEN: Nordbanken economic forecasts for Sweden to 1998.</title>
<headline>Nordbanken economic forecasts for Sweden to 1998.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are forecasts for the Swedish economy from Swedish bank Nordbanken. Figures are percent changes unless specified.</p>
<p>				    1996	1997     1998*</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	1.5	 1.9	3.1</p>
<p> Industrial production	 2.0	 3.5	4.5</p>
<p> CPI, year average	     0.8	 1.3	2.2</p>
<p> Hourly wage increase	  5.7	 4.7	3.9</p>
<p> Savings quota, level	  6.9	 6.2	5.5</p>
<p> Core unemployment, level    7.9	 7.5	6.3</p>
<p> Total unemployment,level   12.5	12.7     12.1</p>
<p> State borrowing (bln SKR)    27	   5	 22</p>
<p> Trade balance (bln SKR)     134	 148	167</p>
<p> Current account (bln SKR)    58	  72	 90</p>
<p> Repo rate			4.35	4.00     5.50</p>
<p> 10-yr bond yield	     7.10	6.75     7.50</p>
<p> DEM/SKR			  4.40	4.40     4.40</p>
<p> USD/SKR			  6.60	6.38     6.16</p>
<p>*=Level for 1998 is only a view, not a forecast, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
